- Non-renewable sources are widely available and can supply power almost anywhere at any time, including continuously.
- Non-renewable fuels are more concentrated and efficient: coal and natural gas can reach about 40% and 60% efficiency, versus 15–20% for solar PV.
- [11] - No energy source can generate electricity 100% of the time.
- Wind and solar, along with battery storage, can add flexibility and predictability that support a reliable grid.
- Renewables contribute to the electricity mix and can help keep power on cost-effectively.
