- No power plant, whether renewable or fossil-fueled, is always available.
- Grids can remain reliable with high shares of variable renewables by combining them with firm renewables, energy storage, and other low-carbon generating sources.
- When solar and wind are low, grids can use transmission over wide areas, storage, demand management, and flexible/backup generation such as geothermal, hydropower, nuclear, or fossil generation with carbon capture.
